  "limitations": [
    "No stable incremental quartet runtime advantage established by overlapping run ranges and mixed paired signs. Median-stage nominal crossover75 is descriptive, not a reliable deployment threshold.",
    "In the actual48-query/plan census, additional quartet setup exceeds the median query saving; preprocessing-inclusive nominal total is slightly worse.",
    "Beta-survivor diagnostic has cheap median57.824ns/query and quartet58.154ns/query; it does not establish a runtime advantage.",
    "All scaling strata with n>=8 have identical cheap-vs-quartet fallback counts. Differences in their runtime medians cannot be attributed to additional quartet pruning.",
    "Several already-cheap-EXACT quartet preprocessing batches are only100--300ns; do not interpret their divided1--5ns values as precise individual call costs.",
    "Common closure was measured explicitly. The timed direct BF consumes the same closed_R; a direct checker can use original ranking edges and avoid closure, but that variant was not timed.",
    "The single-host block schedule reduces drift confounding without proving CPU-load independence, hardware representativeness or population speedup.",
